# Never commit operational state or credentials.
*.env
# The default rehearsal DB capture contains a raw live SQLite pre-image. Keep
# the whole directory unstageable even when an operator runs `git add -A`.
omniroute/rehearsal/private-db/
*.pem
*.key
*-log.jsonl
*.jsonl
# TOG-938's frozen outage samples are a regression fixture, not operational
# state. They must exist in a clean checkout or the stale-feed guards are not
# exercised in CI.
!tests/dead-feed-2026-08-26.jsonl
secure-drop/
*.bak
*.bak-*

# gh-app-token.js writes its minted token here at 0600. The default location is
# $PAPERCLIP_RUN_SCRATCH_DIR, but GH_APP_TOKEN_CACHE can point anywhere, and the
# filename matched none of the patterns above — a LIVE token, one `git add -A`
# from being committed. (TOG-193)
.gh-app-token.json
.gh-app-token.*.json

# Run state the suites drop in the repo root. *.jsonl already covers the queue
# file; these two did not match anything and both survive an interrupted run.
.test-disabled-templates
.provisioner-disabled

# The queue's id-allocation lock (TOG-253) is a DIRECTORY named "<queue>.lock".
# `*.jsonl` does NOT cover it: that pattern matches on the suffix, and this name
# ends in .lock. The lock deliberately survives a killed writer — the next
# writer clears it after a pid liveness check — which is precisely the window in
# which somebody runs `git add -A`. Verified with `git check-ignore`.
*.jsonl.lock
*.jsonl.lock/

# Per-operator agent-harness config. Not a secret, but it is local machine state
# and pins absolute paths that mean nothing on anyone else's checkout.
.claude/

# Installed dependencies for plugins/gh-token-broker. package-lock.json IS
# tracked, so CI installs are reproducible without vendoring the tree. In the
# agent workspace this path is a SYMLINK to the instance plugin root
# (/paperclip/.paperclip/plugins/node_modules) — committing it would either
# commit a dangling absolute symlink or splat the whole instance tree in here.
#   BOTH forms are listed deliberately. A trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES
# ONLY, and git records a symlink as a file, so `node_modules/` alone does not
# ignore the workspace symlink — the exact case the paragraph above is about.
# Verified with `git check-ignore`: with only the slashed form, `ln -s …
# node_modules` shows up as an untracked `?? node_modules` ready to commit.
node_modules
node_modules/

# omniroute-broker's dist/ is hand-written source and is the plugin entrypoint,
# not generated output. Keep this explicit so a future blanket dist/ rule cannot
# silently make the authoritative broker disappear from a fresh clone or CI.
!plugins/omniroute-broker/dist/
!plugins/omniroute-broker/dist/*.js

# Same for dispatch: dist/ is the hand-written entrypoint the manifest points
# at, not a build artefact. Neither is currently ignored, but a blanket dist/
# rule added later would delete the plugin from a fresh clone without failing
# anything visible until an install went looking for the worker.
!plugins/dispatch/dist/
!plugins/dispatch/dist/*.js

# TOG-3354: model-selection's dist/*.js.map are esbuild sourcemaps regenerated
# on every build. Tracking them forces every stacked plugin PR to conflict on
# exactly the .map (the mappings line rewrites wholesale), serialising
# TOG-3012 work. The .js stays TRACKED: plugin_deploy_drift.sh evaluates
# dist/manifest.js straight from git blobs, and the operator BEFORE/AFTER
# bundle copies dist/ from the merged commit with no build step. Maps are
# debug-only (a missing .map never breaks the worker) and rebuild
# deterministically via `npm ci --include=dev && npm run build`.
plugins/model-selection/dist/*.map

# Python bytecode. Until TOG-917 this was covered only BY ACCIDENT: `.claude/`
# above ignores every __pycache__ that happens to sit under a worktree, and
# nothing covered one created next to a tracked .py. CI's own parse gate makes
# them — `python3 -m py_compile` over `omniroute/*.py *.py` — and the "Syntax
# check every script" step cleans up with a hand-maintained
# `rm -rf omniroute/__pycache__ __pycache__`. That list is NOT complete:
# the host-ops broker test imports host-ops/broker.py and leaves a THIRD
# directory, host-ops/__pycache__, behind after the rm has already run.
# Measured, not assumed — five .pyc from the parse gate, one more from the
# broker suite, all `?? `-offered to `git add -A`.
#   Why a compiled artifact is worth a rule: a .pyc carries its source's
# contents. This repo's Python is host-ops/broker.py (reads a management key)
# and the redaction library whose entire job is keeping credential-shaped data
# out of a world-readable file. A stray committed .pyc is a silent second copy
# of code we otherwise review line by line.
#   BOTH forms, for the same reason the node_modules block above gives: the
# trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, so `__pycache__/` alone would miss a
# loose `.pyc` written anywhere else (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE unset plus a
# sys.path entry, or an operator's stray build). Verified with `git check-ignore`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# TOG-1014 fork-disclosure audit: runtime parent cache, host-local
verification/.tog-1014-fork-parents.cache

# Build output for plugins that have a src/ tree. dist/ is rebuilt by CI and the
# release process; it is not tracked.
plugins/model-selection/dist/
plugins/cliproxy-insight/dist/
